  "notes": "A single-beam optical tweezer holding a 150 nm silica sphere in air at 5 mbar, as in levitated optomechanics: 200 mW of 1064 nm light focused by an NA 0.8 objective (an ideal lens, f = 2 mm). Select the screen at the focus and open its Trap tab: trap frequencies of order 100 kHz, softer along the polarisation, and the air’s damping with the quality factor of each motion. At 5 mbar Q is about 50 across the beam. Lower the pressure (Pressure, mbar) and Q climbs in proportion as the gas thins: at 0.01 mbar the sphere rings for tens of thousands of cycles. The Medium is set to Air, so the pressure is the one the sphere feels.",
